We can define a matrix A as follows:
A = [[1, 1], [1, 0]]

Then, we can express the nth Fibonacci number as the top-left element of the matrix A^n.

To compute A^n efficiently, we can use the fast exponentiation algorithm, which has a time complexity of O(log n).

